  "verbalization": "Palmarumycin CP18 appears to interact with MDA-MB-361 through a shared pathway involving 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which acts as a target for multiple entities, including palmarumycin CP18 and Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5. This suggests that palmarumycin CP18 may exert its effects by modulating the activity of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn influences MDA-MB-361. The presence of multiple targets for this compound, including both palmarumycin CP18 and other enzymes, indicates a potential regulatory mechanism where palmarumycin CP18 could act as a modulator or inhibitor of the pathway. The integration of these relationships highlights a possible role for palmarumycin CP18 in targeting the metabolic or signaling pathways that affect MDA-MB-361, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
